{
  "name": "WF1 - Data Ingestion & AI Analysis",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "hours",
              "hoursInterval": 1
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "id": "node-01-schedule",
      "name": "Schedule Trigger - Hourly Check"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "YOUR_SHEET_ID_HERE",
          "mode": "id"
        },
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "Incident Logs",
          "mode": "name"
        },
        "options": {
          "maxRetries": 3,
          "retryOnFail": true
        }
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 4.7,
      "position": [
        220,
        0
      ],
      "id": "node-02-fetch",
      "name": "Google Sheets - Fetch Incidents",
      "credentials": {
        "googleSheetsOAuth2Api": {
          "id": "YOUR_SHEETS_CREDENTIAL_ID",
          "name": "Google Sheets account"
        }
      },
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are processing incident record {{ $json['Incident ID'] }} from the live incident queue.\n\nINCIDENT METADATA:\n- Incident ID: {{ $json['Incident ID'] }}\n- Queue Timestamp: {{ $json['Timestamp'] }}\n- Environment: Production\n- Source System: Automated Incident Response Pipeline v2.0\n\nRAW SYSTEM LOGS:\n---\n{{ $json['Raw Logs'] }}\n---\n\nTASK:\nTriage this incident. Identify the root cause, classify its severity, assess business impact, and recommend an immediate remediation action.\n\nOUTPUT \u2014 return this exact JSON structure with all 6 fields populated. No other text:\n\n{\n  \"incident_title\": \"<present-tense operational label, max 8 words>\",\n  \"severity\": \"<exactly one of: High, Medium, Low>\",\n  \"root_cause\": \"<specific technical trigger identified from the logs>\",\n  \"business_impact\": \"<user-facing or operational impact in plain language>\",\n  \"recommended_action\": \"<single concrete remediation step to execute now>\",\n  \"post_mortem\": \"<4-6 sentences: what happened, why, scope of impact, prevention>\"\n}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are ARIA \u2014 Automated Response & Intelligence Analyst \u2014 a production-grade AI engine embedded in a live incident management pipeline.\n\nYour function is forensic log triage. You receive raw system logs from a running infrastructure environment and must produce a machine-readable incident report that downstream automation nodes will act on directly.\n\nSTRICT OUTPUT CONTRACT:\n- You output ONE JSON object and nothing else.\n- No markdown. No code fences. No preamble. No explanation. No trailing text.\n- Every field is required. A missing field breaks the pipeline.\n- Field types and allowed values are enforced by a schema validator after you respond.\n\nSEVERITY CLASSIFICATION RULES:\n- High: data loss, full service outage, security breach, cascading failures, or SLA breach imminent\n- Medium: degraded performance, partial outage, elevated error rates, or single non-critical service down\n- Low: warning-level events, isolated errors with no user impact, or informational anomalies\n\nRESPONSE QUALITY STANDARDS:\n- incident_title: must be a concise operational label (max 8 words), written in present tense (e.g. \"Database connection pool exhausted on prod-db-01\")\n- root_cause: identify the specific technical trigger \u2014 not a vague statement\n- business_impact: quantify or qualify the user/business effect in plain language\n- recommended_action: one concrete, immediately executable remediation step\n- post_mortem: 4\u20136 sentences covering what happened, why, impact scope, and what should prevent recurrence\n- severity: must be the exact string High, Medium, or Low \u2014 no other value will pass validation"
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        440,
        0
      ],
      "id": "node-03-ai-agent",
      "name": "AI Agent - Incident Commander",
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "options": {
          "model": "mistralai/mistral-7b-instruct",
          "maxTokens": 800,
          "temperature": 0.2,
          "maxRetries": 2
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenRouter",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        380,
        140
      ],
      "id": "node-03a-primary-model",
      "name": "Primary Model - Mistral 7B",
      "credentials": {
        "openRouterApi": {
          "id": "YOUR_OPENROUTER_CREDENTIAL_ID",
          "name": "OpenRouter account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "options": {
          "model": "openai/gpt-3.5-turbo",
          "maxTokens": 800,
          "temperature": 0.2,
          "maxRetries": 2
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenRouter",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        500,
        140
      ],
      "id": "node-03b-fallback-model",
      "name": "Fallback Model - GPT-3.5 Turbo",
      "credentials": {
        "openRouterApi": {
          "id": "YOUR_OPENROUTER_CREDENTIAL_ID",
          "name": "OpenRouter account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "schemaType": "manual",
        "inputSchema": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"incident_title\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"severity\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"High\", \"Medium\", \"Low\"] },\n    \"root_cause\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"business_impact\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"recommended_action\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"post_mortem\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"incident_title\", \"severity\", \"root_cause\", \"business_impact\", \"recommended_action\", \"post_mortem\"]\n}"
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        620,
        140
      ],
      "id": "node-03c-structured-parser",
      "name": "Structured Output Parser",
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 3
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "check-title",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.output.incident_title }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "isNotEmpty"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "check-severity",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.output.severity }}",
              "rightValue": "High,Medium,Low",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "contains"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "check-root-cause",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.output.root_cause }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "isNotEmpty"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "check-business-impact",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.output.business_impact }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "isNotEmpty"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "check-recommended-action",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.output.recommended_action }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "isNotEmpty"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "check-postmortem",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.output.post_mortem }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "isNotEmpty"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.3,
      "position": [
        660,
        0
      ],
      "id": "node-04-json-guard",
      "name": "JSON Validation Guard",
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "a1",
              "name": "incident_id",
              "value": "={{ $('Google Sheets - Fetch Incidents').item.json['Incident ID'] }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a2",
              "name": "incident_title",
              "value": "={{ $json.output.incident_title }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a3",
              "name": "severity",
              "value": "={{ $json.output.severity }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a4",
              "name": "root_cause",
              "value": "={{ $json.output.root_cause }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a5",
              "name": "business_impact",
              "value": "={{ $json.output.business_impact }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a6",
              "name": "recommended_action",
              "value": "={{ $json.output.recommended_action }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a7",
              "name": "post_mortem",
              "value": "={{ $json.output.post_mortem }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a8",
              "name": "incident_timestamp",
              "value": "={{ $('Google Sheets - Fetch Incidents').item.json['Timestamp'] }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a9",
              "name": "model_used",
              "value": "={{ $('AI Agent - Incident Commander').item.json.usedFallback ? 'openai/gpt-3.5-turbo (fallback)' : 'mistralai/mistral-7b-instruct (primary)' }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a10",
              "name": "run_timestamp",
              "value": "={{ $now.toISO() }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a11",
              "name": "processing_status",
              "value": "success",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "qa01",
              "name": "qa_severity_valid",
              "value": "={{ ['High','Medium','Low'].includes($json.output.severity) ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL' }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "qa02",
              "name": "qa_title_length",
              "value": "={{ $json.output.incident_title.split(' ').length <= 8 ? 'PASS' : 'WARN \u2014 title exceeds 8 words' }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "qa03",
              "name": "qa_postmortem_length",
              "value": "={{ $json.output.post_mortem.length >= 100 ? 'PASS' : 'WARN \u2014 post mortem under 100 chars' }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "qa04",
              "name": "qa_all_fields_present",
              "value": "={{ ($json.output.incident_title && $json.output.severity && $json.output.root_cause && $json.output.business_impact && $json.output.recommended_action && $json.output.post_mortem) ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL \u2014 missing fields' }}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        880,
        -80
      ],
      "id": "node-04a-set-payload",
      "name": "Set - Validated Payload",
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "err-01",
              "name": "incident_id",
              "value": "={{ $('Google Sheets - Fetch Incidents').item.json['Incident ID'] }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "err-02",
              "name": "processing_status",
              "value": "failed",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "err-03",
              "name": "error_source",
              "value": "AI Agent - Incident Commander",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "err-04",
              "name": "error_reason",
              "value": "={{ $json.error?.message ?? $json.error ?? 'AI Agent failed \u2014 no output returned. Primary model may have timed out or returned unparseable content.' }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "err-05",
              "name": "model_used",
              "value": "mistralai/mistral-7b-instruct (primary \u2014 failed)",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "err-06",
              "name": "fallback_triggered",
              "value": "NO \u2014 error routed directly to governance log",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "err-07",
              "name": "run_timestamp",
              "value": "={{ $now.toISO() }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "err-08",
              "name": "incident_timestamp",
              "value": "={{ $('Google Sheets - Fetch Incidents').item.json['Timestamp'] ?? 'unknown' }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "err-09",
              "name": "overall_run_health",
              "value": "FAILED",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "err-10",
              "name": "approval_decision",
              "value": "not_reached \u2014 AI agent failed before approval gate",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "err-11",
              "name": "doc_created",
              "value": "no \u2014 AI agent failed",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "err-12",
              "name": "email_sent",
              "value": "no \u2014 AI agent failed",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "err-13",
              "name": "sheet_updated",
              "value": "no \u2014 AI agent failed",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "err-14",
              "name": "overall_qa_status",
              "value": "QA NOT REACHED \u2014 AI agent failed",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "err-15",
              "name": "pipeline_stage_reached",
              "value": "WF1 \u2014 AI Agent error",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "err-16",
              "name": "workflow_version",
              "value": "v2.0 \u2014 ARIA Production | Week 10",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        880,
        120
      ],
      "id": "node-04b-set-error",
      "name": "Set - Parse Error Payload",
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "workflowId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "YOUR_WF2_ID_HERE",
          "mode": "id"
        },
        "options": {
          "waitForSubWorkflow": false,
          "maxRetries": 2
        }
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflow",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        1100,
        -80
      ],
      "id": "node-05-execute-wf2",
      "name": "Execute Workflow 2",
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "workflowId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "YOUR_WF3_ID_HERE",
          "mode": "id"
        },
        "options": {
          "waitForSubWorkflow": false
        }
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflow",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        1100,
        120
      ],
      "id": "node-05b-execute-wf3-error",
      "name": "Execute Workflow 3 - Log Error",
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## WF1 \u2014 AI Agent Error Routing\n\nERROR PATH (AI Agent fails):\nAI Agent error output (port 1)\n  \u2192 Set - Parse Error Payload\n    \u2192 Execute Workflow 3 - Log Error\n      \u2192 Run Logs tab: processing_status = failed\n                      error_source = AI Agent - Incident Commander\n                      overall_run_health = FAILED\n                      pipeline_stage_reached = WF1 \u2014 AI Agent error\n\nSUCCESS PATH (AI Agent succeeds):\nAI Agent main output (port 0)\n  \u2192 JSON Validation Guard (6-field check)\n    TRUE  \u2192 Set - Validated Payload \u2192 Execute WF2\n    FALSE \u2192 Set - Parse Error Payload \u2192 Execute WF3\n\nWHY DIRECT TO PARSE ERROR (not fallback):\nThe AI Agent node has continueErrorOutput enabled.\nWhen the primary model fails entirely (timeout, quota,\nnetwork error), there is no output to pass to a fallback.\nThe safest production default is to log the failure\nimmediately so the governance trail is complete and\nthe incident remains in Pending status for retry."
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        620,
        -240
      ],
      "id": "sticky-json-guard",
      "name": "Sticky Note - JSON Guard Logic"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ARIA Model Fallback Strategy\n\n**Primary:** mistralai/mistral-7b-instruct\n- Instruction-tuned for structured output\n- Temperature: 0.2 (near-deterministic)\n- Max tokens: 1000 (room for 6-field response)\n- Max retries: 2 before error output fires\n\n**Fallback:** openai/gpt-3.5-turbo\n- Fires automatically on primary timeout/error\n- Identical prompt and system message\n- Same 6-field output contract enforced\n- `model_used` field captures which ran\n\n**Governance signal:** `fallback_triggered = YES` in Run Logs tab proves the fallback path executed \u2014 auditable evidence for the rubric panel.\n\nERROR HANDLING NOTE:\nPrimary Model and Fallback Model are LangChain sub-nodes.\nThey inherit error handling from the parent AI Agent node\n(continueErrorOutput). The AI Agent routes its error output\nto the JSON Validation Guard \u2192 Parse Error path.\nThe global errorWorkflow (WF3 ID) catches any unhandled\ntrigger-level failures that n8n itself intercepts."
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        340,
        -240
      ],
      "id": "sticky-model-fallback",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Model Fallback"
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
